WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.580
A gene is cloned; its protein is known.

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.120
But which residue, tail or domain does which job?

3
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.040
A test in a tube can miss a part whose job is to hold a partner.

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.260
Before 1978 there was no widely used way to make a chosen change in a known DNA

5
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.500
sequence. Hutchison, Smith and colleagues introduced one.

6
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.940
Now a site can be tested: necessary, or sufficient?

7
00:00:32.883 --> 00:00:37.783
Pick the residue from a hypothesis, then choose what it becomes.

8
00:00:39.103 --> 00:00:41.183
Alanine cannot accept a phosphate.

9
00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:45.223
Aspartate has a negative charge that imitates one.

10
00:00:46.243 --> 00:00:51.583
A short synthetic DNA oligonucleotide, a primer, carries the change.

11
00:00:51.583 --> 00:01:00.023
In 1978 it was 12 bases long and matched the phiX174 DNA except for the change.

12
00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:04.157
The primer anneals to the single-stranded template.

13
00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:10.137
A DNA polymerase extends it around the circle, and DNA ligase seals it.

14
00:01:11.057 --> 00:01:14.877
Fifteen percent of progeny phage were mutants in 1978.

15
00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:18.797
Kunkel reached 40 to 60% in 1985.

16
00:01:19.977 --> 00:01:24.857
For plasmids, the QuikChange kit copies the whole plasmid with two complementary

17
00:01:24.857 --> 00:01:30.177
mutant primers. DpnI then destroys the methylated parental DNA.

18
00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:37.870
Tyrosine to phenylalanine loses only the hydroxyl, so that tyrosine cannot be

19
00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:44.030
phosphorylated. A kinase-dead mutant changes the lysine that holds ATP.

20
00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:51.010
The receptor can still fold, pair and bind ligand, but cannot transfer phosphate.

21
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.710
A dominant-negative receptor can lack its kinase domain.

22
00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.250
It pairs with normal partners but cannot pass the signal on.

23
00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.970
Compare the mutant with wild type under identical conditions.

24
00:02:05.933 --> 00:02:10.353
A mutant that acts without the signal suggests sufficiency.

25
00:02:11.153 --> 00:02:14.493
One that blocks the normal response suggests need.

26
00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:21.613
In 1988 Feig and Cooper changed H-Ras serine 17 to asparagine.

27
00:02:22.413 --> 00:02:26.013
Its affinity for GTP fell 20- to 40-fold.

28
00:02:27.173 --> 00:02:31.313
Cells with it formed far fewer drug-resistant colonies, so it inhibited

29
00:02:31.313 --> 00:02:34.733
proliferation. Activated ras reversed that.

30
00:02:35.573 --> 00:02:40.653
Cells with v-mos or v-raf resisted it, but v-src cells did not.

31
00:02:41.513 --> 00:02:44.993
That places Ras between Src and Raf in this system.

32
00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:52.087
A mutation can damage folding or expression instead of the chosen function, so

33
00:02:52.087 --> 00:02:55.147
confirm expression and a retained activity.

34
00:02:56.107 --> 00:03:02.447
An aspartate mimic has one charge where phosphate has two, and is smaller, so add a

35
00:03:02.447 --> 00:03:05.267
second line of evidence, such as a kinase inhibitor.

36
00:03:06.627 --> 00:03:11.027
Dominant negatives work through overexpression, which can have effects beyond the

37
00:03:11.027 --> 00:03:16.707
intended block. Use wild-type protein at matching levels, and a rescue, which

38
00:03:16.707 --> 00:03:18.147
restores the blocked response.

39
00:03:19.117 --> 00:03:27.537
In 1987 Kmiecik and Shalloway changed Src tyrosine 527 to phenylalanine.

40
00:03:28.217 --> 00:03:33.997
That strongly activated Src's transforming and kinase activities, and an added

41
00:03:33.997 --> 00:03:37.237
change at tyrosine 416 suppressed them.

42
00:03:38.477 --> 00:03:46.277
In 1993 Struhl, Fitzgerald and Greenwald made truncated Lin-12 and Notch with only

43
00:03:46.277 --> 00:03:47.717
their intracellular domains.

44
00:03:47.717 --> 00:03:53.917
These caused cell-fate changes associated with constitutive activity, independent

45
00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:55.417
of endogenous gene function.

46
00:03:56.267 --> 00:04:04.327
In 1994 Hemmati-Brivanlou and Melton found that a truncated activin receptor turned

47
00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:08.947
Xenopus explants that would become epidermal cells into neural tissue.

48
00:04:09.927 --> 00:04:14.887
That receptor also blocks related ligands, so it blocked more than activin.

49
00:04:16.047 --> 00:04:20.127
Confirm expression and activity, then add a second line of evidence.
